        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): slash replies fail with SecretRef tokens",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users invoking Slack slash commands would receive a generic failure response when the Slack account tokens were configured through SecretRefs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSlack slash handling now selects the active runtime config only when it corresponds to the monitor's config, matching the guarded runtime-config behavior already used by other channel paths. This preserves resolved secret values while still allowing compatible runtime config refreshes between invocations.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSlack slash commands can reply normally when bot and app tokens are supplied through SecretRefs, instead of failing after the command reaches the gateway.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added a regression test covering an unrelated global runtime snapshot containing unresolved Slack token SecretRefs while the monitor holds resolved tokens.\n- Focused validation will be added after PR creation, per repository workflow.",
